{#- Who carries this turn in a group scene (#29). Renders nothing unless
    `speaker` is set: the layer is off by default, and it stays quiet below two
    present NPCs, where naming a lead says only what the cast list already
    said. Selection (direct address, then longest silence) happens in code —
    context/speaker.py; this template receives the nomination.
    Vars: speaker (None | {lead, quiet, reason, spoken, silent_for}). -#}
{%- if speaker %}# Active speaker
{{ speaker.lead }} carries this turn{% if speaker.reason == "named" %} — the last post named them{% elif speaker.reason == "opening" %}{% elif not speaker.spoken %} — they have not spoken yet in this scene{% elif speaker.silent_for %} — they have been silent for {{ speaker.silent_for }} posts{% endif %}.
{% if speaker.quiet %}{{ speaker.quiet | join(", ") }} {{ "is" if speaker.quiet | length == 1 else "are" }} also present: let them react briefly, or not at all. Do not give every character a turn.{% endif %}{% endif -%}
